{"mls":"B1720459","addr":"94 S Forest Road","muni":"Amherst town","town":"Amherst","county":"Erie","zip":"14221","ll":[42.957781,-78.758651],"status":"Active","type":"Single Family","units":1,"beds":4,"baths":2,"sqft":1990.0,"year":1898,"lot":0.74,"dom":12,"price":595000,"orig":null,"chg":"New Listing","tax":7693,"tax_mls":true,"hoa":null,"office":"RE/MAX Plus","phone":"716-989-8734","hhp":false,"remarks":"There is nothing ordinary about 94 S Forest Road—and that is precisely its charm. Behind its stately Victorian exterior is a home that has evolved beautifully without surrendering the details that make it special. Hardwood floors, expansive windows, pocket and French doors, a wood-burning and a gas fireplace, and an elegant formal dining room speak to its past, while abundant natural light, a crisp white galley kitchen and a first-floor full bath with radiant heated floors bring modern comfort into the mix. Two distinct living spaces offer room to spread out, while four bedrooms and a traditional full bath complete the second floor. The home retains the warmth of radiator heat, complemented by mini-split systems for cooling. Nearly three-quarters of an acre creates an unexpectedly private setting, where the flagstone patio becomes a front-row seat to the wildlife that regularly wanders through. And then there is the vintage carriage house—a showpiece all its own. From its wood-burning stove and functioning sliding hay doors to the cupola above, its original character is hard to miss, while the space itself invites endless possibilities for a sports retreat, creative art or hobby studio, private quarters, or additional living space. A home with history, a yard with a personality, a carriage house with a future, and the Village of Williamsville practically at your doorstep—minus the Village taxes. Open house on Friday 10/9, 5-7pm.","facts":[["Total rooms","9"],["Full baths","2"],["Half baths","0"],["Style","Colonial, Victorian"],["Levels","Two"],["Stories","2"],["Bu